For notational convenience, we shall write the Fourier transform $F_f$ as  egin{equation} F_f( m{\omega}) = |F_f( m{\omega})| e^{j 	heta_f( m{\omega})}, \end{equation} with $	heta_f( m{\omega})$ representing the angle. By virtue of the Fourier transform of $f({ m x})$, we have  egin{align} f({ m x}) -f( m{0}) &= \int_{ m{\omega}} e^{j{ m{\omega}}^{	op}{ m x}} F_f({ m{\omega}})\mathrm{d} { m{\omega}} - \int_{ m{\omega}} F_f({ m{\omega}})\mathrm{d} { m{\omega}} 
