otag\ &\overset{	ext{(a)}}{=} \int_{ m{\omega}
e  m{0}}\Big(\cos ig({ m{\omega}}^{	op}{ m x} + 	heta_f( m{\omega}) ig) - \cos ig(	heta_f( m{\omega}) ig)\Big)|F_f({ m{\omega}})| \mathrm{d} m{\omega}, \end{align} where (a) follows since $f({ m x})$ is real-valued. In view of \eqref{eq:Fourier}, we would like to construct a finite collection of features to approximately represent $f( m{x})-f( m{0})$, using the logistic function defined in \eqref{eq:def-func-phi}. Towards this end, we first introduce a quantity related to the difference between $\phi(	au x)$ and the unit step function $\ind(x > 0)$ as follows:  egin{align} \delta_{	au} \coloneqq \inf_{0 < \varepsilon \le 1/2} \Big\{2\varepsilon + \sup_{|x| \ge \varepsilon}  ig|\phi(	au x) - \ind(x > 0)  ig|\Big\}. \end{align} The proof of Lemma ef{lem:discrete} relies heavily upon the following result [Lemma ef{lem:expression}], whose proof is postponed to Appendix~ef{sec:proof:lem:expression}. Next, we would like to obtain a more succinct finite-sum approximation of the integration in \eqref{eq:f-approx-x} via random subsampling. Let us draw $n$ independent samples $(t_i,  m{\omega}_i)$ ($1\leq i\leq n$) from the probability measure $\Lambda(\mathrm{d}t, \mathrm{d} m{\omega})$. Applying the Hoeffding's inequality and the union bound over $\mathcal{N}_{\varepsilon}$ reveals that: with probability at least $3/4$,  egin{align*}  igg| \widehat{f}^{\mathsf{approx}}(\widehat{ m x}) -  rac{1}{n}\sum_{i = 1}^nho_{\widehat{f}}(t_i,  m{\omega}_i)\phi ig(	au(\| m{\omega}_i\|_2^{-1} m{\omega}_i^{	op}\widehat{ m x} - t_i) ig) igg| \lesssim \widetilde{C}_{\mathcal{F}}\sqrt{ rac{\log|\mathcal{N}_{\varepsilon}|}{n}} \end{align*} holds simultaneously for all $(\widehat{f}, \widehat{ m x}) \in \mathcal{N}_{\varepsilon}$, where $\widehat{f}^{\mathsf{approx}}(\widehat{ m x})$ is defined in \eqref{eq:f-approx-x} with $f$ and $ m{x}$ taken respectively to be $\widehat{f}$ and $\widehat{ m{x}}$, and  egin{align} \widetilde{C}_\mathcal{F} \coloneqq C_\mathcal{F} - \sup_{	ilde{f}\in\mathcal{F}}|	ilde{f}({ m 0})|. \end{align} Note that the above application of the Hoeffding's inequality has used the following bounds for any fixed $\widehat{f}$ and $\widehat{ m{x}}$:  egin{align*} \mathbb{E} ig[ho_{\widehat{f}}(t_i,  m{\omega}_i)\phi ig(	au(\| m{\omega}_i\|_2^{-1} m{\omega}_i^{	op}\widehat{ m x} - t_i) ig) ig] &= \widehat{f}^{\mathsf{approx}}(\widehat{ m x}), \  ig|ho_{\widehat{f}}(t_i,  m{\omega}_i)\phi ig(	au(\| m{\omega}_i\|_2^{-1} m{\omega}_i^{	op}\widehat{ m x} - t_i) ig) ig| &\le 3\widetilde{C}_{\mathcal{F}}. \end{align*} Similarly, applying the Hoeffding's inequality and the union bound once again yields that: with probability at least $3/4$,  egin{align*}  igg|\mathbb{E}_{(t,  m{\omega}) \sim \Lambda} ig[ ig|ho_{\widehat{f}}(t,  m{\omega}) ig| ig] -  rac{1}{n}\sum_{i = 1}^n ig|ho_{\widehat{f}}(t_i,  m{\omega}_i) ig| igg| \lesssim \widetilde{C}_{\mathcal{F}}\sqrt{ rac{\log|\mathcal{N}_{\varepsilon}|}{n}} \end{align*} holds simultaneously for all $(\widehat{f},\widehat{ m x})\in\mathcal{N}_\varepsilon$, where we have used the following bound:  egin{align*}  ig|ho_{\widehat{f}}(t_i,  m{\omega}_i) ig| &\le 3\widetilde{C}_{\mathcal{F}}. \end{align*} Thus with probability at least $3/4$, one has  egin{align*}  rac{1}{n}\sum_{i = 1}^n ig|ho_{\widehat{f}}(t_i,  m{\omega}_i) ig| < \mathbb{E}_{(t,  m{\omega}) \sim \Lambda} ig[ ig|ho_{\widehat{f}}(t,  m{\omega}) ig| ig] + \widetilde{C}_{\mathcal{F}}\sqrt{ rac{c_1\log|\mathcal{N}_{\varepsilon}|}{n}} \overset{	ext{(a)}}{\le} 3\widetilde{C}_{\mathcal{F}} + \widetilde{C}_{\mathcal{F}} = 4\widetilde{C}_{\mathcal{F}} \end{align*} simultaneously for all $(\widehat{f}, \widehat{ m x}) \in \mathcal{N}_{\varepsilon}$, where $c_1>0$ is some universal constant, and (a) is valid under the condition that $n\ge c_1\log |\mathcal{N}_{\varepsilon}|$. This further shows that, with probability at least $3/4$, $$ |f({ m 0})| +  rac{1}{n}\sum_{i = 1}^n ig|ho_{\widehat{f}}(t_i,  m{\omega}_i) ig| < |f({ m 0})| + 4\widetilde{C}_\mathcal{F} \le 4C_\mathcal{F} $$ simultaneously for all $(\widehat{f},\widehat{ m{x}})\in \mathcal{N}_{\varepsilon}$. Having established several key properties for the epsilon-cover $\mathcal{N}_{\varepsilon}$, we now extend these properties to all $f\in \mathcal{F}$. For any $f \in \mathcal{F}$, there exists some $(\widehat{f}, \widehat{ m x}) \in \mathcal{N}_{\varepsilon}$, such that for all $\|{ m x}\|_2\le 1$,  egin{align*} & igg|f({ m x}) - f( m{0}) -  rac{1}{n}\sum_{i = 1}^nho_{\widehat{f}}(t_i,  m{\omega}_i)\phi ig(	au(\| m{\omega}_i\|_2^{-1} m{\omega}_i^{	op}{ m x} - t_i) ig) igg|
